  "body": "## What changed\n\n`crates/sim/src/verify/rapids.rs`: the sideways rapid law and #96's vertical dive law now check the tool's whole footprint, not just its centre column. The footprint is a disc of radius r − gouge_tol, sampled at the centre, 8 points at half radius and 16 on the rim. That's the same sampling `rapids_radial.rs` and `hidden_along` already use. A sample is convicted when it lies inside the stock and below what earlier cuts left (`surface_before`). For a sideways rapid this is checked at the start, the midpoint and the end. `acquit_by_prior` already reads the full disc. Sampling limit: a graze shallower than about 0.019·r between two rim points can pass, and the provenance comment says so.\n\n## Pins (`crates/sim/tests/vertical_rapids.rs`, each checked against main)\n\n- `a_dive_centred_half_a_radius_off_the_stock_wall_is_a_rapid_in_stock`: fails on main\n- `a_re_entry_beside_an_earlier_plunge_with_its_far_side_uncut_is_a_rapid_in_stock`: fails on main\n- `a_lateral_rapid_centred_off_the_stock_wall_with_its_rim_in_stock_is_a_rapid_in_stock`: fails on main\n- clean cases: `a_dive_whose_whole_disc_clears_the_stock_wall_is_clean`, `a_dive_touching_the_wall_within_the_gouge_tolerance_is_clean`, `a_lateral_rapid_whose_whole_disc_clears_the_stock_wall_is_clean`\n\n## Readings\n\n92 debug binaries green, SLOW_BINARIES skipped: the sim lib and all 21 sim suites, the app verify-touching suites (including golden_cl, posting and drill_prior), and all non-slow motion binaries. No new conviction appeared in any existing generator output. Clippy on sim and app is clean.\n\nChangelog: Rapid-in-stock checks read the tool's whole footprint, not only its centre: a dive whose rim meets the stock, or a re-entry whose far side is uncut, blocks the post\n\nFixes #106\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
